<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  Fast DDS transport profile for dotFlySim2.
  ============================================================================

  This is THE middleware config for the whole project. RMW_IMPLEMENTATION is
  rmw_fastrtps_cpp everywhere (see the Dockerfile's ENV block), and this file
  is what FASTRTPS_DEFAULT_PROFILES_FILE points at.

  (A note on style: XML forbids a double hyphen inside a comment, so the
  section rules below use '=' and prose uses ';' where you would expect a
  dash. That is a parser rule, not a preference.)

  ============================================================================
  WHAT CHANGED FROM VERSION 1, AND WHY
  ============================================================================
  Version 1 had to reach a DJI Manifold 3 across a wireless LAN. That drove
  three things: a UDPv4 transport with a 1400 byte datagram cap, multicast
  SPDP discovery, and the Manifold named as an explicit unicast peer.

  Version 2 has no Manifold. Every participant (PX4's MicroXRCEAgent,
  ros_gz_bridge, the PSDK bridge, walkerd, RViz, rosbag2, and each C++
  project) lives inside ONE container on ONE host. So:

    1. SHARED MEMORY IS THE TRANSPORT. It is zero copy and it is the only
       thing an in container graph needs. A 6 MB camera frame crosses it
       without touching the IP stack, which is why V1's whole fragmentation
       story (maxMessageSize 1400, DATA_FRAG repair, socket buffer sizing)
       simply does not apply here.

    2. UDPv4 IS KEPT, BUT PINNED TO LOOPBACK. Fast DDS still wants a network
       transport for participant discovery announcements, and some tooling
       behaves better with one present. Confining it to 127.0.0.1 means the
       simulation cannot be discovered from, or leak onto, your LAN.

    3. THERE IS NO MULTICAST. This is the "no multicasting" requirement,
       enforced in two independent places so neither one is load bearing on
       its own:
         a. here, by leaving the default multicast metatraffic locator out
            and giving an explicit loopback unicast locator instead;
         b. in the environment, by ROS_AUTOMATIC_DISCOVERY_RANGE=LOCALHOST,
            which ROS 2 Jazzy applies above the vendor config.

  ============================================================================
  WHY THIS MATTERS BEYOND TIDINESS
  ============================================================================
  Two engineers running V2 on the same office network cannot see each other's
  aircraft, and a stray `ros2 topic pub` on a colleague's laptop cannot fly
  your drone. In V1, on domain 42 with SUBNET discovery, both were possible.

  ============================================================================
  WHY ROS_DOMAIN_ID IS 0 AND NOT 42
  ============================================================================
  Domain 42 existed to share a domain with the Manifold's psdk_wrapper
  container. With discovery confined to localhost the domain number no longer
  isolates anything, so the default is used: one less thing to remember, and
  one less mismatch to debug.

  ============================================================================
  THE SHM SEGMENT SIZE IS LOAD BEARING
  ============================================================================
  32 MB per participant, and V2 runs 8 or more of them. Docker's default
  /dev/shm is 64 MB, which is not enough for even three: the fourth fails with
  "RTPS_TRANSPORT_SHM Error: Failed to create segment" and then silently
  degrades or fails to discover its peers. The container is therefore started
  with 'shm_size=2g', and walkerd checks `df /dev/shm` at start up and warns
  below 512 MB free. If SHM errors ever come back, check THAT first, before
  touching anything in this file.
-->
<dds xmlns="http://www.eprosima.com/XMLSchemas/fastRTPS_Profiles">
  <profiles>

    <transport_descriptors>

      <!-- Shared memory: the real transport for everything in this container.
           segment_size 32 MB comfortably holds the largest frame the composer
           will allow through plus the telemetry churn around it. -->
      <transport_descriptor>
        <transport_id>shm_local</transport_id>
        <type>SHM</type>
        <segment_size>33554432</segment_size>
        <maxMessageSize>65500</maxMessageSize>
      </transport_descriptor>

      <!-- Loopback UDP: discovery announcements, and anything that refuses to
           use SHM.

           interfaceWhiteList takes a concrete local interface ADDRESS.
           127.0.0.1 is the one address guaranteed to exist and guaranteed not
           to be routable off this host.

           A V1 lesson worth keeping, because it cost a day of debugging: this
           element does NOT accept CIDR. An entry of "10.42.0.0/24" matches no
           interface and silently confines the participant to loopback with no
           error message at all. Here loopback IS the intent, so this element
           is finally being used for what it actually does. -->
      <transport_descriptor>
        <transport_id>udp_loopback</transport_id>
        <type>UDPv4</type>
        <interfaceWhiteList>
          <address>127.0.0.1</address>
        </interfaceWhiteList>
        <sendBufferSize>1048576</sendBufferSize>
        <receiveBufferSize>4194304</receiveBufferSize>
      </transport_descriptor>

    </transport_descriptors>

    <participant profile_name="dotflysim2_default" is_default_profile="true">
      <rtps>
        <!-- Only our two descriptors. useBuiltinTransports=false is what stops
             Fast DDS from ALSO creating its default UDPv4 transport on every
             interface, which would undo the loopback confinement above. -->
        <userTransports>
          <transport_id>shm_local</transport_id>
          <transport_id>udp_loopback</transport_id>
        </userTransports>
        <useBuiltinTransports>false</useBuiltinTransports>

        <builtin>
          <discovery_config>
            <discoveryProtocol>SIMPLE</discoveryProtocol>
            <!-- Announce often enough that a unit starting mid session is
                 found quickly; there is no radio link to be frugal for. -->
            <leaseDuration>
              <sec>10</sec>
            </leaseDuration>
            <leaseAnnouncement>
              <sec>3</sec>
            </leaseAnnouncement>
          </discovery_config>

          <!-- THE NO MULTICAST RULE, in the first of its two places.
               Declaring an explicit metatraffic unicast locator on loopback
               replaces the default multicast announcement (239.255.0.1).
               Participants find each other over 127.0.0.1 and nowhere else. -->
          <metatrafficUnicastLocatorList>
            <locator>
              <udpv4>
                <address>127.0.0.1</address>
              </udpv4>
            </locator>
          </metatrafficUnicastLocatorList>

          <initialPeersList>
            <locator>
              <udpv4>
                <address>127.0.0.1</address>
              </udpv4>
            </locator>
          </initialPeersList>
        </builtin>
      </rtps>
    </participant>

  </profiles>
</dds>
